  "title": "Erdős Problem #770",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $h(n)$ be minimal such that $2^n-1,3^n-1,\\ldots,h(n)^n-1$ are mutually coprime.\nDoes, for every prime $p$, the density $\\delta_p$ of integers with $h(n)=p$ exist? Does $\\liminf h(n)=\\infty$? Is it true that if $p$ is the greatest prime such that $p-1\\mid n$ and $p>n^\\epsilon$ then $h(n)=p$?",
